<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guatemala</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guatemala is a region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>, home to Maya peoples and their states. It lay beyond the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>, whose trading and military reach extended towards the region. After the fall of the Aztecs, Spanish forces campaigned into Guatemala, bringing it into the Spanish colonial order.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guatemala.jpg" alt="Guatemala" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: K21edgo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Guatemala.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
